findings.body:
The emitter template was changed in several places beyond the null check, but the regenerated snapshots only pick up the null-check line. In the head revision of `src/OpenApi/gen/XmlCommentGenerator.Emitter.cs` the template emits `operation.Summary = remarks`, `p.Name == propertyName`, and the reordered `RequestBody.Description`. The snapshot `OperationTests.SupportsRouteParametersFromControllers#OpenApiXmlCommentSupport.generated.verified.cs` (and the other updated snapshots) still contain `operation.Description = remarks;` and `p.Name == metadata.Name`.

The generator's output will not match the checked-in snapshots, so `SnapshotTestHelper.Verify` fails for every snapshot test that emits this block. The snapshot is supposed to be a regenerated record of the emitter, so the two cannot be out of sync.

Either the unrelated emitter edits need to go, or the snapshots need to be regenerated from the final emitter source.

::diff{file="src/OpenApi/gen/XmlCommentGenerator.Emitter.cs" lines="380-384"}

::callout{type="warning"}
The snapshot files in this PR were only partially updated. Regenerate them after finalizing the emitter so the snapshot content reflects the emitter output.

The diff deletes the two-line `Licensed to the .NET Foundation…` header from the top of `XmlCommentGenerator.Emitter.cs`. The header has nothing to do with the null-check fix, and the rest of `src/OpenApi/gen` keeps it. Repository license-header checks typically fail on this, and it will show up as noise in the backport.

Restore the header.

::diff{file="src/OpenApi/gen/XmlCommentGenerator.Emitter.cs" lines="1-2"}
